# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization.
#
# eol=lf pins the checkout side as well: text files are written with LF into
# the working tree on every platform, regardless of a local core.autocrlf=true
# (common default on Git for Windows). Blobs were already stored as LF and no
# CRLF blobs exist in history, so this only settles what lands on disk — it
# stops the "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" churn
# and keeps working copies identical between Windows, macOS and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf
